    {
      "id": "o9CR7mG28yFdOE581_QlW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 833,
      "width": 945.4794921875,
      "height": 625,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 41383380,
      "version": 825,
      "versionNonce": 450162796,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788374766279,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1 RPCs - HTTP, gRpc\n    - http - \n        - no strict schema AT all - convention, JSON, etc.\n        - no versioning\n        - modes\n            - request/response. That's it. Synchronous. \n        - stateless \n    - gRPC is better and faster and all that than HTTP. No argument.\n        - strict schema - you have to define the messages you pass\n            - Protobuf - a format for defining messages and endpoints\n        - schema provides versioning\n        - modes\n            - request/response\n            - client streaming to the server (connnected)\n            - server streaming to the client (connected)\n            - both ways (unity) connected\n2 Asynchronous Messaging\n    - queues\n    - fanout\n    - streams\n\n3. Shared Database (it's ok. really. you aren't bad developers. but quit this as soon as you can.)\n\n\n            ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1 RPCs - HTTP, gRpc\n    - http - \n        - no strict schema AT all - convention, JSON, etc.\n        - no versioning\n        - modes\n            - request/response. That's it. Synchronous. \n        - stateless \n    - gRPC is better and faster and all that than HTTP. No argument.\n        - strict schema - you have to define the messages you pass\n            - Protobuf - a format for defining messages and endpoints\n        - schema provides versioning\n        - modes\n            - request/response\n            - client streaming to the server (connnected)\n            - server streaming to the client (connected)\n            - both ways (unity) connected\n2 Asynchronous Messaging\n    - queues\n    - fanout\n    - streams\n\n3. Shared Database (it's ok. really. you aren't bad developers. but quit this as soon as you can.)\n\n\n            ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
